<header class="page-hero short-page-hero">
  <div class="shell page-hero-grid">
    <div><p class="eyebrow"><span></span> Roadmap</p><h1>What is formalized—and what comes next.</h1></div>
    <p>Current work extends reusable foundations in auction theory, pricing, affiliation, and game theory, creating starting points for further research.</p>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="page-section section-rule">
  <div class="shell roadmap-layout">
    <div>
      <p class="roadmap-label"><i class="status-dot complete"></i> Established foundations</p>
      <div class="milestone-list">
        <article><span>01</span><div><h2>Single-parameter problems</h2><p>Envelope incentive compatibility, monotone allocation, payment identities, expected payments, and posted-price optimality.</p></div></article>
        <article><span>02</span><div><h2>Auction theory</h2><p>Symmetric independent private values, revenue equivalence, strict strategy monotonicity, and order-statistic results.</p></div></article>
        <article><span>03</span><div><h2>All-purchase auctions</h2><p>Equilibrium results, explicit bidding strategies, revenue decompositions, algebraic pricing formulas, and expected edition-welfare decomposition with a variance penalty.</p></div></article>
        <article><span>04</span><div><h2>Game-theoretic foundations</h2><p>Normal-form games and pure and mixed Nash equilibrium existence theorems.</p></div></article>
      </div>
    </div>
    <aside class="next-panel">
      <p class="roadmap-label"><i class="status-dot next"></i> On the horizon</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Riley–Zeckhauser comparisons between posted prices and general selling rules</li>
        <li>Posted-price comparative statics</li>
        <li>Connecting the pricing formulas to auction equilibrium outcomes</li>
        <li>Continuous affiliation and winner’s-curse results</li>
        <li>Further game-theoretic integration</li>
        <li>Extensive-form and obviously strategy-proof mechanisms</li>
        <li>Exploratory multi-unit and ascending auctions</li>
        <li>Remove the older website and its archived design files</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="text-link" href="{{ site.issues }}">Follow current work on GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>
